nd for things to get  better but not here alright Emily so  some mixed voices on the streets there  can you tell us more about who the new  Prime Minister is and why he was  selected by Vladimir Putin for this job  well me human true steam has been in  government service for many many years  and he's been the head of the federal  tax service here in Russia since 2010  apparently he has the reputation of a  good manager of an efficient civil  servant a bureaucrat more than a  politician and someone to get the job  done now Putin yesterday announced huge  economic and social reforms along with  the constitutional reforms that he  announced so of what it comes to  internal policy perhaps he just wants  someone who will get the job done and he  knew Steen is a political unknown so no  one will think that he could be a  potential successor to Putin he's not a  political threat in that way he is  however someone known to modernize  things and to digitalize things as well  and he said itself these are big changes  underway in Russia you know political  shake-up and the government also  constitutional changes what is behind  all of this  well mr. shusun became prime minister  because Medvedev resigned yesterday  following Vladimir Putin speech to the  nation where he announced sweeping  constitutional changes including changes  that would strengthen the Parliament  both houses of the Parliament and weaken  the role of the president he also  announced proposed rather changes that  could strengthen the role of the  regional governors around Russia so kind  of decentralized things in Russia a bit  people will have to vote apparently on  these changes in some way Vladimir Putin  and all of these changes that we're  seeing are just are satisfying  a desire amongst Russian people for  change there was a real sense of  stagnation here in Russia up until  yesterday essentially but the main goal  observers say is that Putin is paving  the way for his own political future  Putin's term a current term as president  ends in 2024 he can't run again so  perhaps this is him kind of potentially  creating a new job for himself within a  new political system in the future all  right our correspondent Emily Sherwin in  Moscow thank you
 

